{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make it a requirement for food businesses to provide carbohydrate information",
        "additional_details": "This helps to avoid high/low blood glucose, both of which can be fatal if not acted upon quickly.\r\n \r\nFood vendors don\u2019t always give the essential carbohydrate information needed. People with T1D often need to be careful about where they choose to eat. Only having a rough idea of carbohydrate contents can cause a lot of worry. Everyone with T1D deserves to have the same privileges as everyone else. If this information was provided, it could ease the anxiety that comes with carbohydrate counting.",
        "background": "Currently over 400,000 people in the UK are living with Type 1 Diabetes (T1D), which is very much a life changing autoimmune condition. A big part of living with T1D is carbohydrate counting, to ensure that insulin doses are accurate when eating/drinking.",
